.TH MYGREP 3
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.br
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep
reads lines from the file stream
.I fp
and finds lines containing
.I search_str.
Matching lines are copied into a dynamically allocated array returned through
.I matches.
.PP
The returned array contains one string for each matching line. The caller is
responsible for releasing the allocated strings and the array.
If an input pointer is NULL or a file read error occurs, the function returns -1.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines, or -1 on failure.
.SH AUTHOR
Usman Hassan <usmaanhassan@outlook.com>
